      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Given that the printer prints 17 pages per minute, we need to determine the time required to print 200 pages.\n\nThe time \\( t \\) (in minutes) can be found using the formula: \n\\[ t = \\frac{\\text{Number of pages}}{\\text{Printing speed}} \\]\n\\[ t = \\frac{200 \\text{ pages}}{17 \\text{ pages/minute}} \\]\n\nAfter simplifying, we get:\n\\[ t \\approx 11.76470588 \\text{ minutes} \\]\n\nTo convert this value into the nearest whole number,\nTo convert the decimal to the nearest whole number, round 11.76470588 to the nearest whole number. \n\nTherefore, using the given formula and approximations, we can conclude that it will take \\boxed{12} minutes to print 200 pages.\n\nLet's verify using Python.\n```python\n# Given constants\npages_per_minute = 17\ntotal_pages_to_print = 200\n\n# Calculate the time in minutes needed to print 200 pages\ntime_minutes = total_pages_to_print / pages_per_minute\n\n# Round the result to the nearest whole number\ntime_minutes_rounded = round(time_minutes)\n\nprint(time_minutes_rounded)\n```",
